id: pm-gh1726
title: "GH-1726: a strict boolean extension flag accepts an empty array from direct callers (PmClient.run, the test harness), while {} and 1 are refused"
description: "GH-1726 (filed 2026-11-14). A flag declared value_type boolean with value_validation strict accepts an empty array from direct callers: PmClient.run and the extension test harness's runCommand. The handler receives options.enabled === [] (typeof object) with no warning, while {}, 'bogus' and 1 are refused before dispatch with extension_flag_value_invalid (exit 2). A handler that trusts the host's strict validation, which 2026.11.8+ encourages because the host owns option spelling and value checks, can therefore read a truthy object where it expects true or false. Likely cause from the issue: the empty array is taken as 'no repeated values' and validation is skipped. Expected: a non-repeatable flag never accepts an array; a repeatable boolean flag validates each element and refuses an empty array where at least one value is required. The issue also asks that the changelog name the direct-caller string coercion ('true' -> true) for strict booleans, which broke several fleet test suites between 2026.11.7 and 2026.11.9. Duplicate check: searched strict boolean extension flag empty array direct caller; no open item."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 2
tags[5]: extensions,flags,"gh:1726",sdk,validation
